# Chart colours

Decide first whether colour identifies a source or shows a quantity. In the maintained household charts, a categorical colour identifies a source or device. It must not change because you added another source, hid a series or switched the theme colour. For example, the dishwasher keeps its colour whether or not the oven is shown. Light and Dark remain separate display modes.

The [machine-readable contract](../reference/chart-colours.json) and the repository module `design-system/chart-colours.mjs` give every chart its colours: the theme, the native Energy adapter and the [working examples](../components/chart-examples.html). Do not define another palette inside a chart or demonstration.


## Chart palette

Every chart colour comes unchanged from the GOV.UK chart palette. Colour helps tell categories apart in charts such as line charts and stacked bar charts. In others, such as heatmaps, colour stands for a numeric value.

