## Using colour in charts

- Make sure every colour contrasts enough with the background and with any text on it.
- Never use colour as the only way to show information. Add a label, a pattern, a line style or a table.
- Use colour to make the data clearer.
- Limit the number of colours, so that the chart is not confusing.

Chart colours stay the same in light and dark mode. Some of them have low contrast with the surface, such as Orange tint 25% on white and Blue shade 50% on a dark surface. There, the label, pattern or line style carries the meaning.

